    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "## Problem\n\nDescribe the problem (concisely).\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\n```\nseq 10 | nvim --clean\n```\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/69c447f4-8818-4299-8d0d-2a0811990bd2\n\n## Expected behavior\nExtra cursors lines should be clear after `cc`.\n\n## System info\n\n- Nvim version (nvim -v): `v0.13.0-dev-1661 g4b5dcbccd7` neovim/neovim@4b5dcbccd7\n- Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?: ?\n- Operating system/version: Linux 7.1.8-zen1-3-zen\n- Terminal name/version: kitty\n- $TERM environment variable: `xterm-kitty`\n- Installation: ?\n",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is cosmetic; the insert-mode operation is cascaded after ESC. \n\nFor operations like `o` (an insert \"entry\" command which changes the line-count) this is intentional , to simplify the implementation. ~~But for `cc` (which does not change the line-count) maybe it can live-mirror. Or maybe the entry-command cosntraint is no longer relevant since bd43394d4e6f clarified the heuristic.~~\n\nUpdate: this falls under this `:h mcursor-limitations` item, because `cc` changes the indent of a line:\n\n```\n- During Insert-mode completion, live mirroring pauses if a preview could\n  shift or overlap the primary's completion (same-line edits before the\n  primary, or line insertions/deletions before it).\n```\n\n",
            "created_at": "2026-09-18T08:49:20Z",
